    11	## Task 1: Fix local MCPJam OAuth discovery
    12	
    13	Outcome: success
    14	
    15	Key steps:
    16	
    17	- MCPJam correctly reached `https://mcp-local.skillplane.dev/mcp` and received the expected unauthenticated `401`.
    18	- The `WWW-Authenticate` challenge incorrectly advertised an HTTP metadata URL because the Cloudflare tunnel preserved the public Host while forwarding HTTP to local Wrangler.
    19	- Verified `.dev.vars` and the protected-resource metadata endpoint already used HTTPS; the defect was specifically challenge URL generation under tunneled Host routing.
    20	- Updated `.data/cloudflared.yml` with `originRequest.httpHostHeader: 127.0.0.1:5701` for `mcp-local.skillplane.dev`.
    21	- Validated the tunnel config, restarted the running `skillplane-local` tunnel, and confirmed live discovery.
    22	
    23	Reusable knowledge:
    24	
    25	- Cloudflare tunnel config must override the MCP origin Host header for this local Wrangler setup. Without it, the challenge can downgrade `resource_metadata` to `http://...`, causing hosted MCPJam to return `400 Only HTTPS targets are allowed in hosted mode`.
    26	- After the fix, the live challenge advertised `resource_metadata="https://mcp-local.skillplane.dev/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp"`; protected-resource metadata returned `200` with resource `https://mcp-local.skillplane.dev/mcp` and issuer `https://app-local.skillplane.dev`.
    27	- `apple-touch-icon` 404s are unrelated. Pre-OAuth MCP `401` responses are expected.
    28	
    29	References:
    30	
    31	- `.data/cloudflared.yml`: MCP ingress includes `originRequest: httpHostHeader: 127.0.0.1:5701`.
    32	- Validation: `cloudflared tunnel --config .data/cloudflared.yml ingress validate` returned `OK`.
    33	- Verification: `curl -sS -i https://mcp-local.skillplane.dev/mcp` showed the HTTPS `resource_metadata` challenge.
    34	
    35	## Task 2: Diagnose MCPJam `skill_create` failure
    36	
    37	Outcome: success
    38	
    39	Key steps:
    40	
    41	- The MCPJam browser tab was unavailable, so the diagnosis used local audit/database state and source inspection.
    42	- Audit data showed `workspaces_list` succeeded, but there was no `skill_create` audit event; the request was rejected before tool execution.
    43	- The active `mcpjam test` service credential was inspected: role `editor`, scopes `contexts:read`, `skills:amend`, and `skills:read`.
    44	- `skill_create` requires `skills:write`; `skills:amend` only permits proposing amendments.
    45	
    46	Failures and how to do differently:
    47	
    48	- Do not treat successful MCP connection or `workspaces_list` as proof that mutation tools are authorized. Check the credential’s role and explicit scope for the requested tool.
